{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0194Bf88kPwPmtza7RmU6ZFJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# QuantAgent-e4k — Acceptance Tests: Refactor Backtest to depend only on OrderManager\n2\t\n3\t**Issue:** QuantAgent-e4k  \n4\t**Phase:** Acceptance / Verification\n5\t\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t## AC-1: Backtest has no direct reference to sub-components\n9\t\n10\t**Given** the `Backtest` class after the refactor  \n11\t**When** an instance is created with valid arguments  \n12\t**Then** the instance has no `position_sizer`, `risk_manager`, or `broker` attributes\n13\t\n14\t**Verification:**\n15\t```python\n16\tbt = Backtest(start_date=..., end_date=..., assets=[\"BTC\"])\n17\tassert not hasattr(bt, \"position_sizer\")\n18\tassert not hasattr(bt, \"risk_manager\")\n19\tassert not hasattr(bt, \"broker\")\n20\tassert hasattr(bt, \"order_manager\")\n21\t```\n22\t\n23\t---\n24\t\n25\t## AC-2: OrderManager exposes `reset_daily_tracker`\n26\t\n27\t**Given** an `OrderManager` instance with a mocked `RiskManager`  \n28\t**When** `order_manager.reset_daily_tracker()` is called  \n29\t**Then** `risk_manager.reset_daily_tracker()` is called exactly once\n30\t\n31\t**Verification (unit test):**\n32\t```python\n33\trisk_manager = Mock()\n34\tom = OrderManager(position_sizer=..., risk_manager=risk_manager, ...)\n35\tom.reset_daily_tracker()\n36\trisk_manager.reset_daily_tracker.assert_called_once()\n37\t```\n38\t\n39\t---\n40\t\n41\t## AC-3: OrderManager exposes `close_trade` — success path\n42\t\n43\t**Given** an `OrderManager` with mocked DB, broker, portfolio, and risk_manager  \n44\t**And** the DB returns a `Trade` with `id=1, symbol=\"BTC\", side=BUY, quantity=0.5`  \n45\t**When** `order_manager.close_trade(1, 50000.0, environment=Environment.BACKTEST)` is called  \n46\t**Then** a filled `Order` is returned  \n47\t**And** `broker.place_order` was called with a SELL order for 0.5 BTC  \n48\t**And** `portfolio.execute_trade` was called  \n49\t**And** `risk_manager.on_trade_executed` was called\n50\t\n51\t---\n52\t\n53\t## AC-4: `close_trade` returns None when trade not found\n54\t\n55\t**Given** DB query returns None for the requested `trade_id`  \n56\t**When** `order_manager.close_trade(999, 50000.0)` is called  \n57\t**Then** the return value is `None`  \n58\t**And** no order is placed\n59\t\n60\t---\n61\t\n62\t## AC-5: `close_trade` returns None when risk manager rejects\n63\t\n64\t**Given** a valid trade exists  \n65\t**And** `risk_manager.validate_trade` returns `(False, \"circuit breaker\")`  \n66\t**When** `order_manager.close_trade(1, 50000.0)` is called  \n67\t**Then** the return value is `None`  \n68\t**And** `broker.place_order` is NOT called\n69\t\n70\t---\n71\t\n72\t## AC-6: No regression in existing test suite\n73\t\n74\t**Given** the refactored code  \n75\t**When** the full test suite is run (`pytest tests/ -x`)  \n76\t**Then** all previously passing tests continue to pass\n77\t\n78\t**Key tests to verify:**\n79\t- `tests/test_trading_components.py` — RiskManager, PositionSizer, PortfolioManager\n80\t- `tests/test_order_manager_reversal.py` — existing OrderManager tests\n81\t- Any backtest integration tests\n82\t\n83\t---\n84\t\n85\t## AC-7: `run()` and `run_replay()` still call daily reset via OrderManager\n86\t\n87\t**Given** a Backtest run with mocked OrderManager  \n88\t**When** the backtest processes a new day boundary  \n89\t**Then** `order_manager.reset_daily_tracker()` is called (not `risk_manager.reset_daily_tracker()`)\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a451379-8c79-4d4e-abfc-8730c6577932","uuid":"3dd24a0d-572d-4382-8fb6-a8d043c43eb9","timestamp":"2026-05-12T02:45:14.745Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/05_acceptance_tests/QuantAgent-e4k-AC-refactor-backtest-facade.md","content":"# QuantAgent-e4k — Acceptance Tests: Refactor Backtest to depend only on OrderManager\n\n**Issue:** QuantAgent-e4k  \n**Phase:** Acceptance / Verification\n\n---\n\n## AC-1: Backtest has no direct reference to sub-components\n\n**Given** the `Backtest` class after the refactor  \n**When** an instance is created with valid arguments  \n**Then** the instance has no `position_sizer`, `risk_manager`, or `broker` attributes\n\n**Verification:**\n```python\nbt = Backtest(start_date=..., end_date=..., assets=[\"BTC\"])\nassert not hasattr(bt, \"position_sizer\")\nassert not hasattr(bt, \"risk_manager\")\nassert not hasattr(bt, \"broker\")\nassert hasattr(bt, \"order_manager\")\n```\n\n---\n\n## AC-2: OrderManager exposes `reset_daily_tracker`\n\n**Given** an `OrderManager` instance with a mocked `RiskManager`  \n**When** `order_manager.reset_daily_tracker()` is called  \n**Then** `risk_manager.reset_daily_tracker()` is called exactly once\n\n**Verification (unit test):**\n```python\nrisk_manager = Mock()\nom = OrderManager(position_sizer=..., risk_manager=risk_manager, ...)\nom.reset_daily_tracker()\nrisk_manager.reset_daily_tracker.assert_called_once()\n```\n\n---\n\n## AC-3: OrderManager exposes `close_trade` — success path\n\n**Given** an `OrderManager` with mocked DB, broker, portfolio, and risk_manager  \n**And** the DB returns a `Trade` with `id=1, symbol=\"BTC\", side=BUY, quantity=0.5`  \n**When** `order_manager.close_trade(1, 50000.0, environment=Environment.BACKTEST)` is called  \n**Then** a filled `Order` is returned  \n**And** `broker.place_order` was called with a SELL order for 0.5 BTC  \n**And** `portfolio.execute_trade` was called  \n**And** `risk_manager.on_trade_executed` was called\n\n---\n\n## AC-4: `close_trade` returns None when trade not found\n\n**Given** DB query returns None for the requested `trade_id`  \n**When** `order_manager.close_trade(999, 50000.0)` is called  \n**Then** the return value is `None`  \n**And** no order is placed\n\n---\n\n## AC-5: `close_trade` returns None when risk manager rejects\n\n**Given** a valid trade exists  \n**And** `risk_manager.validate_trade` returns `(False, \"circuit breaker\")`  \n**When** `order_manager.close_trade(1, 50000.0)` is called  \n**Then** the return value is `None`  \n**And** `broker.place_order` is NOT called\n\n---\n\n## AC-6: No regression in existing test suite\n\n**Given** the refactored code  \n**When** the full test suite is run (`pytest tests/ -x`)  \n**Then** all previously passing tests continue to pass\n\n**Key tests to verify:**\n- `tests/test_trading_components.py` — RiskManager, PositionSizer, PortfolioManager\n- `tests/test_order_manager_reversal.py` — existing OrderManager tests\n- Any backtest integration tests\n\n---\n\n## AC-7: `run()` and `run_replay()` still call daily reset via OrderManager\n\n**Given** a Backtest run with mocked OrderManager  \n**When** the backtest processes a new day boundary  \n**Then** `order_manager.reset_daily_tracker()` is called (not `risk_manager.reset_daily_tracker()`)\n","numLines":90,"startLine":1,"totalLines":90}}}
