{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01GXogbgWu96t8JaGTUAEMQp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear understanding of what I need to do:\n\n1. **OrderManager**: Add two methods:\n   - `reset_daily_tracker()` - delegates to `self.risk_manager.reset_daily_tracker()`\n   - `close_trade(trade_id, current_price, environment=None)` - looks up Trade by ID, derives close_side, creates Order, places with broker, updates portfolio, updates risk tracker, commits\n\n2. **Backtest.__init__**: Remove the three lines:\n   - `self.position_sizer = components.position_sizer`\n   - `self.risk_manager = components.risk_manager`\n   - `self.broker = components.broker`\n\n3. **Backtest.run()**: Replace `self.risk_manager.reset_daily_tracker()` with `self.order_manager.reset_daily_tracker()` (line 258)\n\n4. Note: There's no `run_replay()` in the code - only `run()`. The design doc mentioned line 373 for run_replay but it doesn't exist in the code.\n\nAlso, there are import duplications in backtest.py that I should NOT touch (they are not my task).\n\nNow I need to check the Trade model to understand what attributes are available so I can properly implement the close_trade method.\n\nLooking at the Trade model, I need `symbol`, `side`, and `quantity` to close a position. I also need to update the imports in order_manager.py to include `Trade` alongside the existing imports of Order, OrderSide, OrderType, Signal, and TradeSignal.\n\nNow I'm ready to implement the changes to order_manager.py by adding Trade to the imports and then implementing the two new methods.\n\nAdding the reset_daily_tracker and close_trade methods... Finishing up the trade closure by updating the portfolio with the filled order at its average price, then notifying the risk manager and persisting the closed trade record to the database before returning the filled order.\n\nNow I'm reviewing the backtest.py changes needed—removing those three component assignments from `__init__` and updating the daily tracker reset to use the order manager instead of the risk manager directly. I should be careful to only remove what's explicitly requested and leave the imports alone since they might be used elsewhere. I'm debating whether to remove these unused imports proactively or let ruff handle it. The design doc says not to do opportunistic cleanup, but these imports are directly tied to the refactoring—removing the `self.risk_manager`, `self.position_sizer`, and `self.broker` attributes means these classes aren't used anymore. Since ruff will flag and likely fix them anyway during the quality gate, I should just proceed with the explicit changes and let the linter handle the import cleanup.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2689,"cache_read_input_tokens":50236,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2689},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a451379-8c79-4d4e-abfc-8730c6577932","uuid":"cc9f73d4-808c-4d66-9013-315eb8e783a5"}
